es Knight up  here to g5 so Fabiano definitely going  for the aggressive route pawn to h6 and  then nice little move of night to h7 the  rook is kind of forced to take there it  looks bad if you have King to g8 we are  to see if the King goes to e8 then Queen  takes on g7 that's bad  if the King comes to g8 then just Bishop  to h6 you can't take this right here  so maybe plays Knight to g6 trying to  break the pin there other than the  bishop can just take maybe pawn captures  and then Knight to f6 check has to  really take it right here  but then you know Queen takes on g6  checkmate if he doesn't take okay well  then it just gets bad from here we see  King to f7 just starts dropping material  Queen to f3 with the discovered attack  coming maybe now the pawn takes on h6  Knight down here to e4 discovered attack  then after nice of these six things get  pretty dangerous for white here he has  the checkmate threats here on f7 there's  just no way to stop all the threats here  Queen to a5 check pawn to c3 it is  protected by the Queen here on f3 rook  to h7 Castle on the Kings side and in  this position it would be very very  difficult you know for black to really  do too much with this outpost here on d6  with Queen just raised to pounce at any  time it would be very tough for black to  hold on to this so he decides to go  ahead and take with his rook here Bishop  takes on h7 a bishop to a b7 just trying  to get the light square bishop involved  into the game castle on the King side  that Knight to c6 rook here to be one  Bishop down 8 to a6 since it was being  attacked a Bishop to e3 Queen up here to  a5 and then a rook to d1 I really like  to setup from white if you're thinking  about what Fabiana is looking to do it's  an open board state he has double bishop  pair which is always good open board so  you can see the control that he has now  that his bishops can kind of control a  lot of the board you can see both of his  rooks they are on these open files  they're controlling a lot of the  critical squares that Daniel may try to  go to and he has a very active queen  with a safe King if you look up black  side of the board you can see he has a  double pawns on the C file his bishop is  on that the rim over here it's not  really protecting too much it's just  kind of blocked by this pond right here  the Queen's kind of acting alone  both the Knights are playing pretty  defensive and it's rook here on a once  not controlling anything it hasn't moved  too much and the King doesn't have too  much safety so although white is looking  extremely good it's going to be very  very difficult for black to one get out  of this without losing and to find any  sort of way that he can have an attack  to potentially win this game he's really  looking for a drawl like besides to go  ahead and gobble up material here on e5  Queen back to g3 attacking the Knights  and the knight or pawn to f6 protecting  the knight that thing rook up here d6  both attacking material here on e6  getting ready to bring his rook over  here to d1 double-barreling put a lot of  pressure on his opponent but also making  sure that it's on a dark square so the  light square bishop for black can't  really attack it so all in all it's  going to be tough for black to really  stop this defense Bishop a curettage c8  really forced to play defensive here  rook to d1 as we talked about 9 to d5  trying to block off this you know  double-barrel rook here but then Bishop  up here to f4 this works not really  under any threat right now so decides to  go and get it's dark square Bishop  involvement of the game a little bit  more rook to b8 yeah you want to control  a file but not really sure that's going  to be doing too much right now Bishop  takes pawn recaptures and then queen up  to e5 says yeah we'll go and just start  gobbling up other material if possible  and now this opens up the door for them  to put even more pressure on the Kings  side since that night is no longer there  Queen down to d2 that says I have to do  something to try to stop this because  you're threatening the rook up to da  check and then all sort of bad stuff  starts happening rook up to d8 even  after the Queen just says I'm not going  to worry about that King to f7 Bishop to  g8 check King down here to g6 Queen  efore and then after Queen to f3 black  decides to go ahead and resign if we  were to continue we might see Queen up  to f4 but then kind of the dagger move  rook to f8 and the King's forced to move  in at the Queen is going to fall going  to be a pretty easy in game poor Fabiana  Caruana so although we did lose the last  game decided to come back play an  extremely good game  with white against the French defense so  congratulations to him  you know Daniel Plata interesting  variation I think he was a little bit  outclassed in this particular game but I  loved the fact that he was trying  something new always tough to play  Fabiana when he does play the white  pieces playing this well but exciting  game only only about 30 or so moved so  wasn't the longest game but definitely  exciting to watch so hopefully you guys  enjoyed round eight and come back  tomorrow and we'll be looking at round  number 9 thanks for watching

